# Neural Political Compass

A Streamlit-based web application that analyzes political text and matches user stances to political parties using a two-stage neural inference engine. The system leverages SBERT for semantic routing and mDeBERTa for Natural Language Inference (NLI) to evaluate logical alignment, contradiction, and neutrality.

## Ideology & Methodology

The Neural Political Compass operates on the premise of transparent, data-driven political analysis. Traditional political quizzes force users into pre-defined boxes using rigid multiple-choice questions. This project takes a different ideological approach: evaluating a user's organic, free-form text. 

The AI models used (SBERT and mDeBERTa) are inherently neutral logic engines. They do not possess a political stance. The accuracy and ideological mapping of the system are entirely dependent on the quality, breadth, and accuracy of the party stances provided in the `/datasets` directory. The tool is designed for educational, analytical, and exploratory purposes, allowing users to trace exactly *why* a logical entailment or contradiction was flagged. 

IMPORTANT: ANY DATA GATHERED TO TRAIN THE MODELS WILL BE STRICTLY USED FOR THAT PURPOSE. THERE WILL BE NO DATA SELLING.

